WEBVTT

00:01.956 --> 00:03.541
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.624 --> 00:05.366
Desmond said I was gonna die.

00:05.460 --> 00:07.785
He told me he has
these flashes, visions.

00:07.879 --> 00:11.549
When I saw the lightning hit the roof,
you were electrocuted.

00:11.632 --> 00:14.343
When you heard Claire was in the water,
you drowned.

00:14.427 --> 00:15.970
I dove in so you never went in!

00:16.053 --> 00:19.421
No matter what I try to do,
you're going to die, Charlie.

00:19.515 --> 00:23.050
There's a woman in Hurley's tent who
parachuted onto the island yesterday.

00:23.144 --> 00:25.636
The boat she took off from
is 80 miles off the coast

00:25.730 --> 00:29.014
and that if she can find a way
to contact it, we'll all be rescued.

00:29.108 --> 00:32.111
- Why didn't anyone tell me this?
- They don't trust you.

00:32.195 --> 00:34.436
- <i>Kwon is pregnant.</i>
- Where'd you get that?

00:34.530 --> 00:37.074
You're in a position
to be asking us questions?

00:37.158 --> 00:39.233
I told Jack what they were making me do.

00:39.327 --> 00:40.661
Why didn't you tell us?

00:40.745 --> 00:43.372
Because I hadn't decided
what to do about it yet.

01:18.908 --> 01:21.911
Anyone want to guess
as to what Jack's gonna be showing us

01:21.994 --> 01:23.538
out in the middle of nowhere?

01:23.621 --> 01:25.696
I don't know... stuff?

01:26.457 --> 01:28.532
Probably secret stuff.

01:28.626 --> 01:30.701
Why does everything
have to be a secret?

01:30.795 --> 01:33.339
How about some openness for a change?

01:33.422 --> 01:36.509
- We kept the parachute lady secret.
- That's different.

01:36.592 --> 01:38.094
Different how?

01:38.177 --> 01:41.430
Because we weren't out there
playing football with them.

01:41.514 --> 01:44.267
- What?
- Nothing.

01:44.892 --> 01:48.896
Wait. You had one of your flashes
again, didn't you?

01:50.189 --> 01:51.983
No, Charlie. I didn't.

01:54.443 --> 01:55.643
We're here.

02:08.541 --> 02:12.920
A couple of nights ago, Juliet
came to me and she told me everything.

02:13.754 --> 02:17.008
Ben sent her here to find out
which of our women were pregnant.

02:17.091 --> 02:18.916
You guys were doing tests on us?

02:19.010 --> 02:22.294
No. But that's what he wanted me to do.

02:22.388 --> 02:25.673
I've been leaving tapes
at the medical station.

02:25.766 --> 02:29.218
You all heard what he said.
They're coming tomorrow.

02:30.438 --> 02:33.232
Sun, I'm sorry
that I lied to you.

02:34.066 --> 02:36.194
While I appreciate your honesty, Jack,

02:36.277 --> 02:39.614
it doesn't explain
why you brought us out here.

02:42.116 --> 02:43.534
Danielle!

02:52.835 --> 02:54.086
Show them.

03:15.483 --> 03:17.474
When Juliet told me they were coming,

03:18.444 --> 03:20.352
the first thing I thought was,

03:20.446 --> 03:22.938
"Where the hell
are we gonna hide this time?"

03:23.741 --> 03:27.870
But hiding is pointless.
They're just gonna keep coming back.

03:27.954 --> 03:30.957
So I went out and I found some help.

03:31.040 --> 03:35.128
The past few days, she's been bringing
dynamite back from the Black Rock.

03:35.211 --> 03:38.214
For the very first time,
we know exactly what they want,

03:38.297 --> 03:42.343
when they're coming to get it,
and they have no idea

03:42.426 --> 03:44.668
that we're gonna be waiting for them.

03:45.721 --> 03:49.976
So Juliet's gonna mark the tents with
white rocks, just like she was told to.

03:50.935 --> 03:53.729
But there's not gonna be
any pregnant women inside.

03:53.813 --> 03:57.181
There's gonna be plenty
of what we just used on that tree.

03:57.275 --> 04:00.611
So tomorrow night... we stop hiding.

04:00.695 --> 04:03.812
We stop running.
We stop living in fear of them.

04:03.906 --> 04:05.898
Because when they show up...

04:08.452 --> 04:10.611
...we're gonna blow them all to hell.

04:34.103 --> 04:37.137
Bloody hell! Why are we even doing this?

04:37.231 --> 04:40.766
- Chin up, mate. We're headlining.
- Headlining?

04:40.860 --> 04:43.488
We're playing Clitheroe,
the arse end of nowhere.

04:43.571 --> 04:46.324
A gig's a gig.
We're building our fan base.

04:46.407 --> 04:49.608
Will our fan base
pay for a new sodding tire?

04:49.702 --> 04:53.706
Only if we show up.
So let's just get on with it, shall we?

04:53.790 --> 04:57.710
You know what, Liam?
You get on with it. I quit.

04:57.794 --> 04:59.045
You're giving up?

04:59.128 --> 05:02.215
There's nothing to give up on!
We're broke!

05:02.298 --> 05:04.592
The album's not selling!
We're a joke.

05:04.675 --> 05:06.093
Hey! Shut it!

05:06.677 --> 05:08.095
Listen!

05:12.517 --> 05:13.716
That's us.

05:17.230 --> 05:18.481
We're on the radio.

05:22.360 --> 05:25.071
- That we are.
- On the bloody radio!

05:28.115 --> 05:29.659
Oh, yeah!

05:29.742 --> 05:31.869
- Hey!
- Oh! I told ya, baby brother.

05:31.953 --> 05:33.830
We're gonna be bloody rock stars!

05:41.337 --> 05:43.464
Can I ask you something?

05:43.548 --> 05:44.830
Yeah.

05:46.092 --> 05:48.970
Who are you people
about to go to war with?

05:49.053 --> 05:52.087
That's a long story.
Want to ask me something else?

05:52.807 --> 05:55.351
- You having a laugh?
- No, of course not.

05:55.434 --> 05:58.437
I'd never disrespect a fellow Mancunian.

05:58.521 --> 06:01.149
- You're from Manchester, then?
- I am.

06:01.232 --> 06:02.400
My band got its start

06:02.483 --> 06:04.861
at the Night and Day bar
on Oldham Street.

06:04.944 --> 06:07.071
- What band?
- We were called Drive Shaft.

06:07.155 --> 06:11.242
- Yeah, yeah. I know you.
- We had our moment in the sun.

06:11.325 --> 06:14.036
No, not that. The crash.
You're the dead rock star.

06:14.120 --> 06:16.956
They made a big deal out of you
when they found the plane.

06:17.039 --> 06:20.293
- Huge memorial service, new album...
- There's a new album?

06:20.376 --> 06:23.629
Yeah. God, it was everywhere.
A greatest hits thing.

06:28.968 --> 06:33.546
Hey, look on the bright side.
You're not really dead, right?

06:34.891 --> 06:36.058
Yeah, right.

07:00.374 --> 07:04.504
We need more wire so that we can trigger
these from a safe distance.

07:04.587 --> 07:07.548
I can get people to start stripping
the plane wreckage.

07:07.632 --> 07:11.584
We should be able to finish rigging
these tents in the next 24 hours.

07:11.677 --> 07:13.669
We'll be ready by tomorrow night.

07:19.352 --> 07:21.844
- We need to talk about Naomi's phone.
- Not now.

07:21.938 --> 07:25.441
If you are angry I doubted you,
I'll make an apology later. But now...

07:25.525 --> 07:27.985
Look, I'm a little bit
busy right now, Sayid.

07:28.069 --> 07:30.530
And I'm trying
to get us off this island, Jack.

07:34.116 --> 07:35.910
I can't transmit using this phone

07:35.993 --> 07:39.664
because Danielle's distress signal
is overriding the frequency.

07:39.747 --> 07:41.791
If you tell me where the radio tower is,

07:41.874 --> 07:44.335
I can switch off your message
and call for help.

07:44.418 --> 07:48.339
My signal has been playing for the last
16 years and nobody has heard it.

07:48.422 --> 07:53.334
- What makes you think you'll have luck?
- Naomi's boat is 80 miles offshore.

07:53.427 --> 07:56.597
I know if we eliminate
Danielle's signal, they'll hear us.

07:56.681 --> 07:58.589
No, they won't.

07:58.683 --> 08:00.977
And why is that?

08:01.060 --> 08:02.801
- We're jamming it.
- What?

08:02.895 --> 08:04.887
Ben is using one of the Dharma Stations

08:04.981 --> 08:07.942
to block all of the signals
off of the island except ours.

08:08.025 --> 08:11.227
- What station?
- They call it the Looking Glass.

08:11.320 --> 08:13.698
- The Looking Glass?
- Yes, it's underwater.

08:13.781 --> 08:16.023
I have no idea where it is.

08:17.368 --> 08:18.953
I believe I do.

08:19.954 --> 08:22.988
Look, I know Jack thinks it's best,

08:23.082 --> 08:25.324
but what if they're coming
for him again?

08:27.670 --> 08:29.255
Claire, listen to me.

08:29.338 --> 08:32.842
I'm going to protect you.
I'm going to protect Aaron.

08:34.302 --> 08:38.087
I promise.
Everything is going to be fine.

08:42.393 --> 08:44.635
Sorry.

08:44.729 --> 08:47.815
Charlie, can you give me
a hand with something?

08:48.900 --> 08:51.986
Yeah, Desmond, of course.

09:04.707 --> 09:07.376
So, you ready to tell me
what you saw this morning?

09:07.460 --> 09:08.795
Aye.

09:10.254 --> 09:13.090
Right. So how does it happen this time?

09:16.344 --> 09:19.680
Come on, Des.
You can tell me. I can take it.

09:24.644 --> 09:27.188
What I saw, Charlie, was...

09:27.897 --> 09:31.015
...Claire and her baby
getting into a helicopter...

09:31.108 --> 09:36.614
...a helicopter that...
that lifts off, leaves this island.

09:42.703 --> 09:44.831
- Are you sure?
- Aye.

09:45.832 --> 09:50.128
Rescue helicopter? On this beach?
This island? That's what you saw?

09:52.797 --> 09:55.007
We're getting bloody rescued?

09:55.091 --> 09:58.052
I thought you were gonna tell me
I was going to die again!

10:02.682 --> 10:04.267
You are, Charlie.

10:06.018 --> 10:07.520
Wait. What?

10:09.105 --> 10:12.441
If you don't, none if it will happen.

10:14.443 --> 10:16.654
There won't be any rescue.

10:19.407 --> 10:23.359
I'm sorry, brother.
But this time...

10:25.955 --> 10:28.166
This time you have to die.

10:37.049 --> 10:40.219
Come on. Come on.

10:41.429 --> 10:43.973
Come on. Come on, Charlie.

10:44.056 --> 10:46.809
Jump in. I'm gonna catch ya, boy.

10:46.893 --> 10:50.010
No. You're just gonna back away.

10:50.104 --> 10:52.148
Don't be daft. Jump in.

10:53.691 --> 10:57.059
- No!
- I promise. I'm gonna catch ya!

10:57.153 --> 10:58.863
No, he won't!

10:58.946 --> 11:00.531
Zip it, you!

11:01.866 --> 11:05.453
Don't listen to your brother.
Just jump on in.

11:07.789 --> 11:10.541
There's nothing
to be afraid of, Charlie.

11:10.625 --> 11:14.462
I'll catch ya. I promise.

11:36.818 --> 11:38.694
I did it!

11:39.487 --> 11:41.562
- You got it!
- I did it!

11:41.656 --> 11:45.326
You're swimming, Charlie!
You're swimming.

11:51.874 --> 11:53.459
What're you writing?

12:00.466 --> 12:01.634
Nothing.

12:09.517 --> 12:11.644
All right, tell me.

12:13.646 --> 12:15.064
You sure you want to know?

12:17.525 --> 12:21.936
- It might be easier if you just...
- Yeah. I want to know.

12:26.075 --> 12:28.870
You're inside a hatch. It's...

12:30.329 --> 12:32.071
...a room full of equipment.

12:32.790 --> 12:36.075
There's a blinking yellow light
above a switch.

12:36.169 --> 12:38.045
You flick the switch.

12:39.964 --> 12:42.592
The light goes off.

12:47.305 --> 12:48.890
And then you drown.

12:59.859 --> 13:01.277
When?

13:04.113 --> 13:05.312
I don't know.

13:05.406 --> 13:08.910
You're sure you saw Claire and Aaron
get on that helicopter?

13:08.993 --> 13:10.244
Aye.

13:12.622 --> 13:14.332
So...

13:15.583 --> 13:18.377
...before I... drown,

13:19.796 --> 13:21.453
I just have to flick the switch?

13:23.341 --> 13:24.509
That's right.

13:29.222 --> 13:30.598
Where is it then?

13:35.269 --> 13:38.554
This is the Looking Glass.
It's an underwater Dharma station.

13:38.648 --> 13:42.068
Please, can you tell me anything
you might know about this place?

13:42.151 --> 13:45.154
I've never been down there.
I don't know anyone who has.

13:45.238 --> 13:47.031
Why not?

13:47.698 --> 13:51.869
There was some accident. Ben told us
that the station was completely flooded.

13:51.953 --> 13:55.706
- If it's flooded how does it work?
- How it still works is irrelevant.

13:55.790 --> 13:58.251
The question is
how do we get it to stop working,

13:58.334 --> 14:00.242
so we can use the satellite phone.

14:02.547 --> 14:06.717
The diagram shows that the Looking Glass
is connected to the island by a cable.

14:06.801 --> 14:10.002
I feel sure that this is
the very same cable down the beach

14:10.096 --> 14:11.514
which runs into the ocean.

14:11.597 --> 14:14.559
If we follow the cable,
it should lead us to the station.

14:14.642 --> 14:18.010
- So how're we gonna get in?
- We swim in.

14:18.104 --> 14:19.438
There's a moon pool,

14:19.522 --> 14:22.556
a room with an open floor
at the base of the station,

14:22.650 --> 14:24.892
big enough for a submarine to dock.

14:24.986 --> 14:26.612
Even if the station's flooded,

14:26.696 --> 14:29.730
I think I'll be able to find
the relay switch and disable it.

14:29.824 --> 14:31.482
What about swimming back out?

14:32.869 --> 14:34.151
No.

14:34.245 --> 14:37.947
I'm not letting you go on some
suicide mission just to flip the switch.

14:38.040 --> 14:40.918
Someone has to do it,
or we'll never leave this island.

14:41.002 --> 14:42.378
I'll do it.

14:42.462 --> 14:45.829
Swim down, turn off that switch,
swim back up. Piece of cake.

14:45.923 --> 14:48.082
You don't know what we're talking about.

14:48.176 --> 14:51.762
I was junior swim champion.
I can hold my breath for four minutes.

14:51.846 --> 14:54.640
I know exactly
what you're talking about, Jack.

14:58.478 --> 15:00.605
No. And there's no reason
to do this now.

15:00.688 --> 15:02.398
We're gonna focus on the Others,

15:02.482 --> 15:04.139
- then deal with this.
- Wait.

15:04.233 --> 15:06.141
We have a chance
to signal for a rescue.

15:06.235 --> 15:09.572
For 90 days, I've been asked
to make decisions for this camp.

15:09.655 --> 15:11.866
There you go. I just made one.

15:21.167 --> 15:24.170
Rose, that's a sailor's hitch.
It's not gonna hold.

15:24.253 --> 15:27.590
- You wanna do a sheet bend like mine.
- Now you're a knot expert?

15:27.673 --> 15:30.635
Well, trust me, it's...

15:34.472 --> 15:36.547
How did you do that?

15:36.641 --> 15:39.268
Watch and learn, dear, watch and learn.

16:43.249 --> 16:46.419
Hey! Look, there! Look!

17:02.727 --> 17:05.271
- Get off him! It's OK!
- What?! He's one of them!

17:05.354 --> 17:07.482
I know! I know, it's OK.

17:08.983 --> 17:12.601
He was in the cage next to me!
I know this guy!

17:12.695 --> 17:15.406
What the hell are you doing here, Karl?

17:15.490 --> 17:18.576
They're... coming. My people...

17:18.659 --> 17:21.235
Sorry you came all this way,
but we already know.

17:21.329 --> 17:22.789
Then why are you still here?

17:22.872 --> 17:25.708
When your people
show up here tomorrow, we're ready.

17:25.792 --> 17:28.993
Tomorrow? No!
No, they're coming tonight!

17:35.718 --> 17:37.710
They're coming right now!

17:46.187 --> 17:47.303
Hey!

17:50.900 --> 17:53.277
- When'd you get back?
- Just now.

17:55.363 --> 17:57.657
Where's Locke?

17:59.617 --> 18:01.035
Here's your gun back.

18:06.374 --> 18:09.043
- Ben, what's going on?
- Where's Ryan?

18:09.127 --> 18:12.130
- He's at his tent. Are you alone?
- It's time to get them.

18:12.880 --> 18:16.665
- Wait a minute. But you said tomorrow.
- Jacob wants it to happen now.

18:16.759 --> 18:19.001
What happened out there?
Did John see...?

18:19.095 --> 18:20.596
John had an accident.

18:23.015 --> 18:24.840
- Ryan!
- Yes, sir.

18:25.852 --> 18:29.355
If you leave now, how long
will it take you to reach their camp?

18:29.438 --> 18:31.983
If I take my ten best
we can hit them by nightfall.

18:32.066 --> 18:35.517
- Then you better get going.
- No, Ben. Moving up the schedule...

18:35.611 --> 18:37.519
Juliet may not be ready. What if...

18:37.613 --> 18:39.740
Then we'll take all their women.

18:40.908 --> 18:43.661
And we'll sort out
the ones we need later.

18:43.744 --> 18:44.912
And the men?

18:44.996 --> 18:48.781
If any of them are stupid enough
to get in your way, kill them.

18:48.875 --> 18:51.002
All right.

19:03.139 --> 19:04.932
Karl!

19:06.601 --> 19:08.102
It's me.

19:11.481 --> 19:14.984
- I thought you were bringing rabbit.
- You have to go. Now.

19:15.067 --> 19:16.861
What? Did he find out I was out here?

19:16.944 --> 19:19.864
No. He's sending Pryce
to their beach camp right now.

19:19.947 --> 19:21.532
- You warn them!
- Warn them?

19:21.616 --> 19:24.191
- Go now!
- They were gonna take pregnant women.

19:24.285 --> 19:27.538
Take the outrigger, you'll get there
a few hours before them.

19:27.622 --> 19:30.500
- Wait, Alex.
- He's gonna kill them, Karl!

19:32.960 --> 19:36.464
Austen and Ford saved your life.

19:39.717 --> 19:40.916
You owe them.

19:44.222 --> 19:45.765
You'd better take this.

19:48.976 --> 19:51.354
If I get caught,
your father's gonna kill me.

19:51.437 --> 19:53.095
Is he my father?

20:01.989 --> 20:03.731
Now, go.

20:29.559 --> 20:31.602
- Is that everything?
- Yeah.

20:33.938 --> 20:35.137
Do you trust him?

20:35.231 --> 20:37.556
You don't trust me? What about her?

20:37.650 --> 20:39.975
She's a spy.

20:40.069 --> 20:43.906
She's supposed to mark the tents
of the pregnant women with white rocks.

20:43.990 --> 20:47.274
They know, Karl. But, thanks.

20:47.994 --> 20:50.830
- So what're we gonna do?
- We have to leave now, hide.

20:50.913 --> 20:54.500
Where? It's their island.
If they wanna kill us, they'll find us.

20:55.877 --> 20:59.161
Sun's gonna go down in a few hours.
We have enough wire yet?

20:59.255 --> 21:00.371
Not even close.

21:00.465 --> 21:03.092
We gotta figure out a way
to set the dynamite off.

21:03.176 --> 21:05.303
- We can shoot.
- We don't have enough guns.

21:05.386 --> 21:08.264
- He said that ten of them are coming.
-The tents.

21:08.347 --> 21:10.756
We camouflage the dynamite
next to the tents,

21:10.850 --> 21:13.342
target it from our positions
at the tree line.

21:14.353 --> 21:18.649
Juliet marked three tents.
That means we need three guns.

21:19.567 --> 21:21.944
Here. You can have mine, too.

21:23.029 --> 21:24.853
I'll be your third.

21:25.823 --> 21:28.451
We'll take your gun,
but you're not staying here.

21:30.453 --> 21:33.028
You're gonna lead everyone
to the radio tower.

21:33.122 --> 21:34.665
Radio tower?

21:34.749 --> 21:38.033
We can't risk losing the chance
to contact with Naomi's boat.

21:38.127 --> 21:41.130
So everything has to happen
at the same time.

21:43.216 --> 21:46.719
Charlie, you still up for a swim?

21:50.097 --> 21:51.557
Yeah, I believe I am.

21:53.226 --> 21:55.301
I'll go with him.

21:55.394 --> 21:58.272
OK. We better get to it.

22:14.664 --> 22:17.416
It's here, baby brother!
Christmas is here!

22:20.169 --> 22:21.911
Are these the birds from row two?

22:23.923 --> 22:25.383
Well done, mate.

22:31.347 --> 22:33.589
Well, as you have spent another year

22:33.683 --> 22:36.227
as the only drug-free rock star
in the world,

22:36.310 --> 22:39.021
I am going to share
a little known fact with you.

22:41.399 --> 22:44.652
Father Christmas lives
just down the street from here.

22:44.735 --> 22:47.697
- Father Christmas lives in Helsinki?
- Indeed he does.

22:47.780 --> 22:50.105
In case you haven't noticed,
baby brother,

22:50.199 --> 22:52.493
Finland is the bloody North Pole.

22:54.162 --> 22:58.875
Therefore, a very special gift for you
this year.

23:04.630 --> 23:06.841
Liam, no. Mum gave you that.

23:06.924 --> 23:08.509
You're the first born.

23:08.593 --> 23:11.512
It was her father's
and his father before that...

23:11.596 --> 23:13.055
And it's a family heirloom,

23:13.139 --> 23:16.726
and that's why we named the band
after Dexter bloody Stratton. I know.

23:16.809 --> 23:18.968
But Charlie, let's be honest.

23:20.438 --> 23:22.429
We both know I'm a sodding mess.

23:22.523 --> 23:24.932
But you, you're different.

23:25.026 --> 23:29.071
You're gonna get married,
have a family, a baby.

23:30.990 --> 23:33.566
- I'll be lucky if I hit 30.
- Don't say that, Li.

23:33.659 --> 23:37.246
The ring has to stay
in the family, Charlie.

23:38.247 --> 23:41.949
So please, take it.

23:43.085 --> 23:45.296
Mum would've wanted it this way.

23:45.379 --> 23:47.705
Pass it on to your little one someday.

23:47.799 --> 23:50.343
I need to know it's safe.

23:57.016 --> 23:59.174
I'll hold on to it.

24:01.646 --> 24:03.637
But I won't take it.

24:06.692 --> 24:10.060
Hey, it fits. Look at that.

24:10.154 --> 24:12.062
Happy Christmas, baby brother.

24:43.646 --> 24:44.929
You need some help?

24:46.399 --> 24:48.891
Why didn't you tell me
you were going to do this?

24:54.949 --> 24:56.409
I didn't want you to worry.

24:57.952 --> 25:01.873
Well, it's dangerous, isn't it,
swimming into some underwater station?

25:01.956 --> 25:05.658
It's what needs to be done
to get us all rescued.

25:07.003 --> 25:08.994
I'll be fine, Claire.

25:10.465 --> 25:12.289
You gotta promise me something.

25:13.634 --> 25:15.178
While I'm gone...

25:18.139 --> 25:19.599
...don't worry about me.

25:23.936 --> 25:25.135
OK.

25:32.820 --> 25:34.019
I'll take him.

25:36.157 --> 25:37.325
Thanks.

25:38.326 --> 25:39.827
Hey...

25:44.415 --> 25:46.626
All right, turnip head.

25:47.752 --> 25:52.079
You take care of your mum,
while I'm away, OK?

26:01.599 --> 26:02.975
I love you.

26:22.161 --> 26:23.412
See you soon.

26:27.375 --> 26:30.826
Be careful, Charlie. OK?

26:30.920 --> 26:32.171
Yeah.

27:25.850 --> 27:28.144
I'm sorry, guys.
Thanks, man.

27:38.404 --> 27:40.646
Help! Help me!

27:40.740 --> 27:45.234
Help! Please! Please!

27:47.830 --> 27:49.572
- You, stop!
- Hey!

27:49.665 --> 27:51.542
Get the hell away from her!

27:52.168 --> 27:54.712
What're you doing? Leave her alone!

27:57.548 --> 27:59.175
You OK, miss?

27:59.258 --> 28:01.584
Yes. I think so, yes.

28:03.471 --> 28:05.097
Here you go.

28:06.182 --> 28:08.173
Pardon me while I have a heart attack.

28:08.267 --> 28:10.895
Last time I was in a fight,
I was eight years old.

28:13.231 --> 28:14.607
And I lost.

28:15.525 --> 28:19.737
Well, that makes you
even more of a hero, doesn't it?

28:19.821 --> 28:24.450
- I just did what anyone would do.
- Three people walked by the alley.

28:25.326 --> 28:26.911
- What?
- They saw me...

28:26.994 --> 28:29.288
...but they just kept on going.

28:31.332 --> 28:33.574
You are a hero, sir.

28:33.668 --> 28:37.839
And don't let anyone
ever tell you differently.

28:53.896 --> 28:55.721
- What's that?
- It's weight belt.

28:55.815 --> 28:58.734
It should bring you down
quicker than swimming.

28:59.902 --> 29:01.445
Well, every second counts.

29:03.281 --> 29:05.272
So I just take it off when I hit bottom,

29:05.366 --> 29:08.984
swim up through the moon pool
into the station,

29:10.079 --> 29:13.916
swim into whichever room has
the yellow blinking switch,

29:14.750 --> 29:15.866
flip it.

29:18.671 --> 29:19.954
Nothing to it.

29:24.552 --> 29:27.180
So how long can you really
hold your breath for?

29:29.849 --> 29:31.507
Does it matter?

29:38.649 --> 29:41.850
- You want me to hit another one?
- No. You've made your point.

29:41.944 --> 29:44.947
Bernard, this is not pheasant hunting
in Montgomery.

29:45.031 --> 29:47.700
- I know what I'm doing.
- Pheasants don't shoot back.

29:47.783 --> 29:51.871
Nothing's gonna happen to me, Rose.
I just have to shoot a tent.

29:51.954 --> 29:55.625
- And I'll be right behind you.
- Then I'm staying, too.

29:55.708 --> 29:57.335
No, you're not, Rose.

29:58.795 --> 30:01.756
Everyone's gathering down
at the south end of the beach.

30:01.839 --> 30:04.217
- No one's staying but the shooters.
- Says who?

30:04.300 --> 30:08.137
You wanna give me your word that
nothing's gonna happen to my husband?

30:08.221 --> 30:09.555
Then I'll go.

30:11.432 --> 30:14.884
If we don't kill everyone
who shows up here in about an hour,

30:14.977 --> 30:17.104
it's not gonna matter where Bernard is.

30:18.689 --> 30:23.569
I like you better since you got back,
Jack. You're almost an optimist.

30:23.653 --> 30:24.737
Come on.

30:24.821 --> 30:28.866
If you're gonna be hiding in the bushes,
let's get you into something dark.

30:31.744 --> 30:33.162
You better get going.

30:33.246 --> 30:36.165
Rousseau says it's a day's walk
up to the radio tower.

30:36.249 --> 30:38.543
I'm not taking them to the tower,
you are.

30:40.837 --> 30:43.131
- Excuse me?
- You're not staying behind.

30:44.549 --> 30:47.218
- This was my idea.
- I'm capable of executing it.

30:47.301 --> 30:50.179
- I owe them!
- What are you more concerned with?

30:50.263 --> 30:53.599
Killing the Others
or getting our people off this island?

30:55.726 --> 30:58.135
This afternoon
you said you were our leader.

31:03.276 --> 31:05.153
It's time for you to act like one.

31:09.157 --> 31:12.118
Lead them to the radio tower, Jack.

31:13.911 --> 31:15.736
And then take us all home.

31:26.799 --> 31:28.759
Dudes! Wait!

31:31.596 --> 31:32.795
I heard.

31:32.889 --> 31:35.975
I heard what you're doing.
I wanna come with.

31:38.352 --> 31:42.440
Everyone, they're all goin'
to the radio tower,

31:42.523 --> 31:46.444
and I'm sick of trekking,
and, you know, explosions.

31:47.987 --> 31:51.855
I think I can help you guys out.
I'm a really good paddler.

31:58.581 --> 31:59.832
You can't go, Hurley.

32:01.459 --> 32:02.658
Why not?

32:05.379 --> 32:06.756
Because...

32:09.008 --> 32:12.626
...you're too big.
You won't fit in the boat.

32:20.686 --> 32:22.063
That's uncool, man.

32:24.857 --> 32:28.444
Wait! Wait! Wait!

32:30.446 --> 32:33.731
Dude. It's fine. I don't even
wanna go on your stupid boat.

32:39.539 --> 32:41.280
I'll catch up with you later.

32:41.958 --> 32:45.409
- Just remember I love you, man.
- Yeah, whatever. I love you, too.

33:02.436 --> 33:04.261
You got water in there? Good. Good.

33:04.689 --> 33:07.066
How about you? Lot of water? Good.

33:08.317 --> 33:09.433
Hey.

33:10.736 --> 33:13.447
- Hey.
- So here we go again.

33:15.158 --> 33:17.201
Here we go again.

33:20.079 --> 33:24.083
- The tents are all marked. We're set.
- Sayid find a third shooter?

33:35.094 --> 33:37.638
Ready, Claire?
Need a hand with the little guy?

33:37.722 --> 33:39.682
No thanks, I'm OK.

33:46.898 --> 33:49.275
How's my little sweetheart?

33:51.944 --> 33:55.312
We're just gonna go for a little walk,
so hold on to Mum, OK?

34:19.138 --> 34:20.681
This is it.

34:28.022 --> 34:29.680
Ready?

35:42.972 --> 35:44.515
Hiya.

35:44.599 --> 35:46.590
Do you want a blanket?

35:46.684 --> 35:48.060
Oh, thanks, I've got one.

35:49.395 --> 35:52.356
Well, you're warming for two. Take mine.

35:54.066 --> 35:55.182
Thank you.

36:04.285 --> 36:07.288
So, first plane crash?

36:08.748 --> 36:12.335
- What gave it away?
- You can always spot the newbies.

36:17.340 --> 36:19.550
We're gonna be OK, you know.

36:21.010 --> 36:22.512
Are we?

36:22.595 --> 36:26.213
We're alive, on a beautiful island.

36:27.433 --> 36:29.018
We'll sleep under the stars,

36:29.101 --> 36:33.147
and before you know it, the helicopters
will come and take us all home.

36:34.357 --> 36:36.150
You really think they'll find us?

36:37.276 --> 36:39.351
Well, yeah, why wouldn't they?

36:41.072 --> 36:42.240
Thanks.

36:45.159 --> 36:47.484
- I'm Charlie.
- I'm Claire.

36:48.538 --> 36:51.332
- Nice to meet you, Charlie.
- It's nice to meet you.

37:12.854 --> 37:14.730
We're here.

37:25.283 --> 37:27.691
I want you to give this
to Claire for me.

37:33.583 --> 37:35.168
What is it?

37:39.464 --> 37:42.467
It's the five best moments of my...

37:43.468 --> 37:45.793
...sorry excuse for a life.

37:48.723 --> 37:50.099
My greatest hits.

37:55.480 --> 37:57.440
You know...

38:00.234 --> 38:04.405
...memories... are all I've got.

38:06.240 --> 38:08.148
You don't have to do this, Charlie.

38:09.327 --> 38:10.495
What?

38:12.663 --> 38:16.751
- I'll go.
- No, your flashes...

38:16.834 --> 38:20.838
Maybe I keep seeing you die
because...

38:22.840 --> 38:25.082
...l'm supposed to take your place.

38:30.723 --> 38:33.757
What about your girl? Penny?

38:36.229 --> 38:37.688
What about your girl?

38:42.193 --> 38:43.611
Besides...

38:47.740 --> 38:50.451
...I might be luckier than you.

38:59.043 --> 39:00.837
Keep your memories to yourself.

39:05.049 --> 39:06.509
I'll take it from here.

39:14.183 --> 39:15.601
I don't know what to say.

39:19.272 --> 39:21.732
Well, you can tell me
where the weight belt is.

39:23.276 --> 39:24.652
Right there behind you.

39:50.928 --> 39:55.673
You and I both know you're not
supposed to take my place, brother.

42:00.266 --> 42:04.051
I'm alive. I'm alive!
